
Thanks
======

Some people and projects have helped more, some less, but nevertheless
everyone's help has been important. :-)

Projects and Organizations:
  - Brave Software (https://brave.com/)
      For creating the Brave browser, the Brave Shields engine, and
      maintaining an outstanding open-source privacy browser ecosystem.
  - The Chromium Authors & Google (https://chromium.googlesource.com/)
      For developing and maintaining the Chromium browser engine and Blink.
  - GitLab (https://gitlab.com/)
      For providing generous, powerful Continuous Integration and Continuous
      Deployment (CI/CD) SaaS runners, Generic Package Registry, and GitLab
      Pages hosting that power Braving's automated build and updater systems.
  - Raymond Hill (gorhill) & uBlock Origin (https://github.com/gorhill/uBlock)
      For developing uBlock Origin, advanced procedural cosmetic filtering,
      scriptlet injection standards, and privacy filter lists.
  - EasyList & EasyPrivacy Community (https://easylist.to/)
      For maintaining primary ad-blocking and privacy protection filter lists.
  - Ryan Brown (Fanboy)
      For maintaining Fanboy's Annoyance, Social, and Mobile notification lists.
  - Peter Lowe / Blocklist Project (https://pgl.yoyo.org/adservers/)
      For maintaining foundational host-based advertisement server lists.
  - The Rust Project (https://www.rust-lang.org/)
      For the fast and memory-safe language powering Brave Shields' adblock-rust.
  - LLVM & Clang Team (https://llvm.org/)
      For the high-performance compiler infrastructure used across all platforms.

Maintainers and Contributors:
  - gajgaje2000 <gajgaje2000@gmail.com>
  - Cerium Browser Team

Also thanks to all users and community members who test Braving releases,
submit bug reports, and help improve the browser.

I have probably forgot to add some names or projects to the above list.
Sorry about that and thanks for your help.

